From 226a5113cc3c1d5a6af6838b9aed995b74ba6985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:32:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [TSReader] Keep TS timestamps exact across segments, and seek
 TS streams to the key frame

The TS demuxer, the TS sample reader and the WebM reader take the PTS
offset of each frame from the segment of the frame. The TS reader also
seeks to the PES of the key frame before the seek time, and plays the last
frames of a segment and of the stream. The demuxer tests share the
AdaptiveStream copy with the ADTS tests and build as one executable with
generated TS segments.

Requires the ADTS patch for the shared test executable and the ADTS frame
reads.

- Fix the timing offset of HLS audio, TS video and WebM streams after
  each segment change, which was one or more frames wrong until the next
  seek
- Fix a seek in a live TS stream that aligned the other streams to the
  time before the seek when the next segment was not available yet, and
  end a TS stream after a seek past the end
- Fix a seek in a TS stream that continued at the key frame after the
  seek time, or at the next segment, instead of at the key frame before
  the seek time
- Fix a seek in a TS stream to the last frames of a segment, or to a
  time between two frames, which continued at a later key frame
- Fix the end of a TS stream, which did not play the last video frames
  and the audio of the last PES
- Fix the timing offset of TS audio that follows the video of the next
  segment, of the first TS audio frames before the first video frame,
  and of TS and WebM segments with only one frame
- Fix a seek in a TS audio stream that continued at the first frame of
  the PES instead of at the frame of the seek time
- Fix a seek in a TS stream with video and audio that continued at the
  key frame before the key frame of the seek time
- Fix a seek in a TS stream with video and audio that returned an audio
  frame first, so the other streams aligned to the audio time instead of
  the video frame of the seek
- Fix a seek in an HEVC or MPEG-2 TS stream, which continued at the
  segment start instead of at the key frame of the seek time
- Fix the end of an HEVC TS stream after a PES without data, which did
  not play the last frame
- Fix the timing offset of a TS segment whose first PES header starts in
  the segment before
- Fix a seek in an H.264 or HEVC TS stream to a key frame that uses the
  parameter sets of an earlier frame, which ended the stream
- Fix a seek in an MPEG-2 TS stream to an I picture without a sequence
  header, which continued at the next sequence header
- Fix a seek in a TS stream to a key frame whose PES starts in the
  segment before, which continued at the next key frame and lost the
  audio of a PES across the two segments
- Fix reads past the data, crashes and wrong decoder setups from H.264
  and HEVC TS streams with corrupt parameter sets, an H.264 SPS longer
  than 256 bytes, an HEVC parameter set after a 3 byte start code, or an
  HEVC VPS in another TS packet than the PPS
- Fix a seek in a TS stream to a key frame whose PES starts at the end
  of the segment before with no frame data or only the first bytes of
  the frame, which continued at the next key frame
- Fix a live seek to a key frame whose PES starts in the segment before,
  which lost the first audio frame of an audio PES across the two
  segments while the seek waited for the next segment
- Fix a seek in a TS stream to a key frame whose PES starts in the
  segment before, which dropped the frames after that key frame up to
  the next key frame
- Fix the timestamps of TS video and audio frames that the parser read
  only after the next PES started, which took the PTS of the next frame,
  as with HEVC access unit delimiters or parameter sets in a PES of
  their own, or with an audio frame header across two PES
- Fix the last frame of a TS segment or stream whose parameter sets came
  in a PES of their own, which was read as two frames
- Fix a seek in a TS stream to a key frame whose picture PES starts in
  the next segment, which returned that key frame twice
- Fix a live seek in a TS stream that waited more than once for the next
  segment, which lost audio frames of an audio PES across the two
  segments
- Fix a TS AAC stream with a corrupt ADTS header whose frame length is
  shorter than the header, which stopped the playback in an endless loop
  or sent a corrupt frame
- Fix TS audio in PES packets without a PTS at the start and after a
  seek, which had no PTS up to the next PES with a PTS, also in the next
  segment, and could not be the target of a seek, and a key frame in a
  PES without a PTS after a seek, which took the PTS of a later frame
- Fix a TS AAC stream with a corrupt ADTS or LATM header whose frame
  length leaves no frame data, which stopped the playback in an endless
  loop or sent an empty frame that moved the audio clock, and an ADTS
  sync word in the data with no valid sample rate, which could hide the
  next frames
- Fix MPEG-2 and MPEG-2.5 Layer III TS audio (MP3 at 24 kHz or less),
  which joined each two frames into one sample with the wrong
  timestamps, the timestamps of Layer I TS audio, and the channel count
  of mono MPEG TS audio
- Fix the timestamps of AAC frames with more than one raw data block in
  TS and HLS packed audio, and of LATM frames with more than one sub
  frame
- Fix the timing offset of a TS audio segment whose first PES has no
  PTS, which was off by the frames before the first PTS, and the
  timestamps of TS audio frames across the 33 bit PTS wrap before the
  first PTS and inside a PES
- Fix the timestamps of TS E-AC-3 frames with fewer than 6 blocks, and
  of 7.1 channel TS E-AC-3, and send both substreams of a frame as one
  sample, also when a segment ends between the substreams

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
